  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IGAD 2018-2023 IPPSHAR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IGAD, 2018-2023, IPPSHAR - IGAD 2018-2021 IPPSHAR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EU-kommissionen har beslutat att avs&#xe4;tta totalt 40 miljoner euro fr&#xe5;n EU:s Sk &quot;Emergency Trust Fund&quot; f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja genomf&#xf6;randet av IGAD:s freds- och s&#xe4;kerhetsstrategi under perioden 2018-2022, varav 5 miljoner Euro kommer g&#xe5; till l&#xf6;nekostnader och 35 miljoner euro tilldelas &apos;IGAD Promoting Peace and Stability in the Horn of Africa Region&apos;, IPPSHAR-programmet. Programmets riktning &#xe4;r helt i linje med den svenska strategin och dess fokus p&#xe5; f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt kapacitet bland regionala akt&#xf6;rer f&#xf6;r fred och f&#xf6;rsoning, &#xf6;kat kvinnligt deltagande i fredsprocesser och bek&#xe4;mpning av v&#xe5;ldsbejakande extremism. Sverige kommer att tilldela 10,5 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av programmet, pengarna kommer att st&#xe4;llas till f&#xf6;rfogande f&#xf6;r anv&#xe4;ndandet av &#xd6;sterrikes Bist&#xe5;ndsorgan, ADA, som &#xe4;r utsedd som partner ansvarig f&#xf6;r  genomf&#xf6;rande av det delegerade EU-avtalet och Sidas bidrag. ADA bidrar med ytterligare 1 million Euro till programmet och Nederl&#xe4;nderna bidrar med ca 600.000 euro. Insatsens totala summa &#xe4;r d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r 42,6 miljoner euro.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EU Commission has decided to allocate a total of EURO 40 million from the EU Trust Fund to support the implementation of IGAD&apos;s Peace and Security Strategy during the period 2018-2022, of which 5 million euro will go to salary costs and 35 million will go to the &apos;IGAD Promoting Peace and Stability in the Horn of Africa Region, IPPSHAR, programme.The direction of the programme is fully in line with the Swedish strategy, and its focus on strengthened capacities among regional actors for peace and reconciliation, increased women&apos;s participation in processes for peace, and combating of violent extremism. Sweden will allocate 10,5 MSEK for the implementation of the programme, the funds will be made available for the use of  the Austrian Development Agency (ADA) who has been appointed as the managing agent of the delegated EU-agreement as well as Sida&apos;s contribution. ADA is contributing an additional 1 million euro to the IPPSHAR programme and the Netherlands is contributing with 676,579 euro. The total contribution amount is therefore 42.6 million euro.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The General objective is &quot;to contribute to achieving sustainable peace, security and stability for the attainment of economic integration and development in the IGAD region (Djibouti, Eritrea, Ethiopia, Kenya, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan and Uganda).&quot; The Four specific objectives are:

1. To enhance the IGAD Conflict Early Warning and Response Mechanism (CEWARN) systems, so that there is an improvement in the quantity and quality of the information collected, in data analysis, and early response action
2. To enable IGAD and national governments in the region to predict, prevent, and address transnational security threats
3. To enhance the capacity of IGAD and national governments of the region on preventive diplomacy, mediation and civilian peace building
4. To enhance the implementation effectiveness of IGAD&apos;s Peace and Security Division (PSD) and units</narrative>
  </description>
